<title>INDIA: India's BPCL 96/97 1st half net up.</title>
<headline>India's BPCL 96/97 1st half net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   2,068.0   vs	 1,929.0</p>
<p>    Gross turnover    81,735.0   vs	68,631.0</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees) *     27.58  vs	    25.71</p>
<p>Net sales/income</p>
<p>    from operations   48,805.0   vs	40,172.0</p>
<p>    Other income	   755.0   vs	   879.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 44,769.0   vs	36,574.0</p>
<p>    Interest		 323.0   vs	   210.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 1,330.0   vs	 1,136.0</p>
<p>    Tax		    1,070.0   vs	 1,202.0</p>
<p>Note: The state-run Bharat Petroleum Corporation Ltd (BPCL) is one of India's three leading oil refiners. The figures are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
